<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<LanguageData>

  <!--
    The manage-policies window inherits RimWorld's own layout, which reads both of these through
    Translate. They are keys rather than literals so a translation of this mod has somewhere to put
    its version of them.

    Both are held to the shape of the vanilla policy windows on purpose, and the tip has a hard
    ceiling behind it: Dialog_ManagePolicies gives the tip a rect exactly 32px tall, sitting at a
    fixed offset with the panels below it. Widgets.Label clips to that rect, so a tip that runs to a
    second line is cut off mid sentence with nothing in the log to say so. One line, and the length
    of vanilla's own policy tips is the safe bound.

    What is deliberately not said here: that tightening a policy never disarms anybody. It is true
    and it is worth knowing, but it does not fit, and a control that describes its own edge cases is
    not the house style anyway.
  -->
  <Gideon_WeaponPolicyTitle>Weapon policies</Gideon_WeaponPolicyTitle>
  <Gideon_WeaponPolicyTip>Create and manage templates for controlling which weapons colony members can carry.</Gideon_WeaponPolicyTip>

</LanguageData>
